## What this session accomplished

**Started from:** criteria.json showed the full 1/2/4/8/16/32 caw matrix green, but on mixed builds spanning six days. I completed run68 (third consecutive dir_reuse_coherency@32/caw pass on 0.10.66, probe sweep clean across all 32 rings) and began re-validating the whole matrix on one build — which immediately exposed real bugs the mixed-build history had been masking.

**Four root-caused fixes (0.10.67→0.10.70), each RULE-4 instrumented:**

1. **noino release fence impatience** (0.10.67): posix_multi's 3200-file `ls` storm made 5 nodes simultaneously misdiagnose a slow-but-advancing AIL as wedged and self-shutdown. Fence is now progress-based (wedges only on a provably frozen AIL min).
2. **FLUSHING dead-end AIL freeze** (0.10.68, proven by the new P-AILMIN dump): fresh inode-cluster buffers carry `_XBF_DELWRI_Q|_XBF_MXFS_ALLOC_QUEUED`, which xfsaild can never write; create-only workloads never trigger the AG-release drains that land them. The fence now drains the mxfs alloc buflists on stall. Result: posix_multi, mmap_coherency, zero_silent_loss all went 0/32 → **32/32 PASS**.
3. **Stale async release stripping fresh grants** (0.10.69/70): a queued no-inode release executing after its node re-acquired the lock cleared the new tenure's slot bit — proven double-EX (two nodes converting the same dir 4ms apart) and 15K "held-miss" events per 3 minutes. Added gen-anchor + in-core liveness re-checks + acquire-side serialization; dlm_scaling@32 then passed 32/32 (run73).
4. Built fast tooling: `scripts/mkdir_storm.sh` (reproduces the concurrent-mkdir dirent loss in 1-5 rounds), `probe_sweep.sh`, `revalidate_cell.sh`, `matrix_check.py --since` (the honest YES gate).

## Where it stands

The storm repro still loses one dirent by round 5 on 0.10.70: the shared parent converted shortform→block **five times in one incarnation**, each EX holder reloading a stale dinode — the dinode-durability handoff (or its reader-side adopt) is the remaining hole. The exact next probe is documented in memory (`AAA-ccloopdaf5-sess1-END-storm-loss-chain-4-fixes-next-probe-durable-gating`): check the gating around `mxfs_dlm_dir_inode_durable` at xfs_inode.c:2236-2340, then either the enforcement's pin-bail budget or reader monotonicity. After that bug falls: g2@32, dir_reuse@32 on the final build, then the 16/8/4/2/1 ladder re-run and the `matrix_check --since` gate before any YES marker.

